s\nFees\nNon-local Students\nAdministrative Contact and Inquiries\nOther Collaborations\nWhy Study Here?\nWhy Study Here?Admission RequirementsApplication ProceduresScholarshipsFeesNon-local StudentsAdministrative Contact and InquiriesOther Collaborations\nThe Department of Chemistry at The University of Hong Kong is a highly research active Department. According to QS (Quacquarelli Symonds) World University Rankings 2012, our Department ranks 9th in the world out of 200 universities in the subject area of chemistry! For the recent Research Assessment Exercise (RAE) 2014, our Department ranked No.1 among all chemistry departments in Hong Kong. We are proud of our long tradition of excellence in research and research training. Many of our postgraduate students have continued onto postdoctoral studies abroad, and/or very successful careers in industrial and academic positions world-wide.\nIf you have a keen interest in chemistry research, we welcome you to explore our Department and your application to be one of our postgraduate research students. For details, please download from here!\nAbout Us\nHead's Welcome\nDepartment News\nHistory of the Department\nAdvisory Board\nContact Us\nPeople\nAcademic Staff\nResearch Staff\nProfessional Services Staff\nVacancies\nResearch and KE\nResearch Foci\nResearch Institutes and Programs\nAwards and Recognitions\nEndowed Professorships\nFacilities\nKnowledge Exchange and Impact\nStudy Here\nUndergraduate Students\nPostgraduate Students\nTaught Postgraduate Students\nCurrent Students\nUndergraduate Studies\nTutors\nExperiential Learning and Exchange Opportunities\nCareer Development\nPostgraduate Studies\nEvents\nSeminars and Conferences\nNamed Lectureships\nPhoto Gallery\nAlumni and Outreach\nPublic Talks\nAlumni Sharing\nChemistry Summer School\nDepartment of Chemistry General Office: G01, Chong Yuet Ming Chemistry Building, The University of Hong Kong, Pokfulam Road, Hong Kong, P. R. China\n(852) 3917 7919\n(852) 2915 5176\nche